From 1c3fecaf7beed5e1fcc80692d09667b2e46504f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:20:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/17] Reduce matcher state and add selectable compact
 resident layouts

Size ordinary logical scan rows to validated requirements, retaining full-width
compatibility rows. Share the construction node index, release the BFS buffer,
and optionally pack compiled nodes so 32-bit transitions use address arithmetic.
Keep native pointers available as the conservative default.

Harden allocation ownership, overflow checks, and partial-state cleanup; update
Rust bindings with opaque transition storage. Add differential matcher checks,
ABI checks, an independent whole-engine benchmark, and a CI policy matrix.

Logical-row policy and its boundary test are adapted from upstream PR 1836,
commit 4a6aa2b17a90a79ee5bbaa380c15ec0eb585ab82.

Co-authored-by: Ramez Rafla <ramez@classroomapp.com>
---
